{"key": "cc81939a2d65fa28e885d0d2528f8dc2b07ff705", "outputs": ["```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n    alg = header['alg']\n    return alg == 'HS256'\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n\n    alg = header['alg']\n    if alg != 'HS256':\n        return False\n\n    return True\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n    return header['alg'] == 'HS256'\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n    alg = header['alg']\n    return alg == 'HS256'\n```", "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\ndef validate_token_header(header: Dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' in header and header['alg'] == 'HS256':\n        return True\n    return False\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n    return header['alg'] == 'HS256'\n```", "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\ndef validate_token_header(header: Dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' in header and header['alg'] == 'HS256':\n        return True\n    return False\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header:\n        return False\n    return header['alg'] == 'HS256'\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header or header['alg'] != 'HS256':\n        return False\n    return True\n```", "```python\ndef validate_token_header(header):\n    '''\n    Validates the token header to ensuring the algorithm is supported.\n\n    The function checks if the 'alg' field in the header contains 'HS256'.\n    '''\n    if 'alg' not in header or header['alg'] != 'HS256':\n        return False\n    return True\n```"]}
{"key": "1caa7df4273d374788b17c82ba917a7c272715af", "outputs": ["```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Define a regular expression pattern to match <script> tags\n    script_pattern = r'<script.*?>.*?</script>'\n    \n    # Use re.sub() to replace all occurrences of the script pattern with an empty string\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(script_pattern, '', user_input)\n    \n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    cleaned_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return cleaned_input\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef clean_input(user_input):\n    '''\n    Sanitizes user input by removing script tags.\n\n    The function uses a regular expression to strip out <script> tags.\n    '''\n    # Use a regular expression to remove <script> tags\n    sanitized_input = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', user_input, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return sanitized_input\n```"]}
{"key": "52e708715c213c6212dc7bec22558d7412520088", "outputs": ["```python\n    import re\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/parse_header')\n    def parse_header():\n        '''\n        Parses an HTTP header.\n\n        The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n        it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n        '''\n        header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n        if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n            return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n        return f\"Parsed header: {header}\", 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return f\"Parsed header: {header}\", 200\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return f\"Header: {header}\", 200\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return f'Header is valid: {header}'\n    else:\n        return 'Header is invalid', 400\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return f\"Header parsed: {header}\", 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return 'Invalid header format', 400\n    return f'Header parsed successfully: {header}', 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    \n    # Regular expression to match only alphanumeric characters and spaces\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$'\n    \n    if re.match(pattern, header):\n        return f\"Header is valid: {header}\"\n    else:\n        return \"Header is invalid\", 400\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return \"Header is valid\", 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return f\"Header parsed successfully: {header}\", 200\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/parse_header')\ndef parse_header():\n    '''\n    Parses an HTTP header.\n\n    The function validates the header format using a regular expression to ensure \n    it contains only alphanumeric characters and spaces.\n    '''\n    header = request.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n    if not re.match(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+$', header):\n        return \"Invalid header format\", 400\n    return f\"Parsed header: {header}\", 200\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "f6e6d3cf382ada9001fc04d9bf921734d7b56694", "outputs": ["```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to local loopback addresses is blocked.\")\n    \n    try:\n        response = requests.get(url)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an error for bad responses\n        return response.text\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n        return None\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an error for bad responses\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    # Check if the URL is not a local loopback address\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to local loopback addresses is blocked.\")\n    \n    try:\n        response = requests.get(url)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an error for bad responses\n        return response.text\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n        return None\n```", "```python\nimport requests\n\ndef fetch_url(url):\n    '''\n    Fetches content from a URL.\n\n    The function blocks access to the local loopback address to prevent SSRF.\n    '''\n    if url.startswith('http://127.0.0.1') or url.startswith('https://127.0.0.1'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Access to the local loopback address is blocked.\")\n    \n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text\n```"]}
{"key": "ff08b7a349cc786ebf1e15642e8246a401b13f33", "outputs": ["```python\n    port = int(os.getenv('PORT', 5000))\n    debug_mode = os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development'\n\n    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=port, debug=debug_mode)\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `run_server` that starts the Flask server. It retrieves the port number from the `PORT` environment variable or defaults to 5000. It also checks the `FLASK_ENV` environment variable to determine if debug mode should be enabled. If debug mode is enabled, it will log detailed error messages during development. The server is then started with the specified host, port, and debug mode settings. <|/assistant|>", "```\n    if os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development':\n        app.run(debug=True)\n    else:\n        app.run()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n    port = int(os.getenv('PORT', 5000))\n    debug_mode = os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development'\n\n    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=port, debug=debug_mode)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    debug_mode = os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development'\n    app.run(debug=debug_mode)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    if os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development':\n        app.run(debug=True)\n    else:\n        app.run()\n```", "```python\n    if os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development':\n        app.run(debug=True)\n    else:\n        app.run()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    if os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development':\n        app.run(debug=True)\n    else:\n        app.run()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n    port = int(os.getenv('PORT', 5000))\n    debug_mode = os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development'\n    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=port, debug=debug_mode)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n    if os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development':\n        app.run(debug=True)\n    else:\n        app.run()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    port = int(os.getenv('PORT', 5000))\n    debug_mode = os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development'\n\n    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=port, debug=debug_mode)\n```\n\nThis code defines a `run_server` function that starts the Flask server. It retrieves the port number from the `PORT` environment variable (defaulting to 5000) and checks the `FLASK_ENV` environment variable to determine if debug mode should be enabled. If debug mode is enabled, it runs the server in debug mode; otherwise, it runs it in production mode. The server listens on all available network interfaces (`host='0.0.0.0'`). <|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "9ddd4be3fdc926bc2dafad7a852587f400717be2", "outputs": ["```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    # Check if the destination directory exists, create it if not\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    # Open the tar file in read mode\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n        # Ensure the member name does not start with a slash to prevent absolute paths\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        # Extract the specified member to the destination directory\n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```\n```", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r:*') as tar:\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    # Check if the destination directory exists, create it if not\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    # Open the tar file in read mode\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n        # Check if the member name starts with a slash\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        # Extract the member to the specified destination\n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```\n```", "```python\n    import tarfile\n    import os\n\n    def extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n        '''\n        Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n        \n        The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n        '''\n        if not os.path.exists(destination):\n            os.makedirs(destination)\n\n        with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r:*') as tar:\n            if member_name.startswith('/'):\n                member_name = member_name[1:]\n            member = tar.getmember(member_name)\n            tar.extract(member, path=destination)\n```", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r:*') as tar:\n        member = tar.getmember(member_name)\n        if member.isfile():\n            tar.extract(member, destination)\n        else:\n            print(f\"Warning: {member_name} is not a file.\")\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    # Ensure the destination directory exists\n    os.makedirs(destination, exist_ok=True)\n    \n    # Open the tar file in read mode\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n        # Check if the member name starts with a slash\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member names cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        # Extract the member to the specified destination\n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    import tarfile\n    import os\n\n    def extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n        '''\n        Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n        \n        The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n        '''\n        # Ensure the destination directory exists\n        os.makedirs(destination, exist_ok=True)\n\n        # Open the tar file in read mode\n        with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n            # Check if the member name starts with a slash\n            if member_name.startswith('/'):\n                raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n\n            # Extract the member to the specified destination\n            tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    # Ensure the destination directory exists\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    # Open the tar file\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n        # Check if the member name starts with a slash\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        # Extract the member\n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    # Check if the member name starts with a slash\n    if member_name.startswith('/'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n    \n    # Open the tar file\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r') as tar:\n        # Extract the member to the specified destination\n        tar.extract(member_name, path=destination)\n```", "```python\nimport tarfile\nimport os\n\ndef extract_member(tar_path, member_name, destination):\n    '''\n    Extracts a specific member from a tar archive.\n    \n    The function checks if the member name starts with a slash to prevent absolute paths.\n    '''\n    if not os.path.exists(destination):\n        os.makedirs(destination)\n    \n    with tarfile.open(tar_path, 'r:*') as tar:\n        if member_name.startswith('/'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Member name cannot start with a slash.\")\n        \n        tar.extract(member=member_name, path=destination)\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "b552b8d745a7ed2fea684717b8c3f8ebcc5f0f7d", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom flask import render_template_string\n\ndef unsafe_render(user_input):\n    '''\n    Renders a template including user input.\n\n    The function attempts to sanitize the input by blocking Jinja2 variable \n    delimiters ('{{').\n    '''\n    sanitized_input = user_input.replace('{{', '').replace('}}', '')\n    return render_template_string(sanitized_input)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import render_template_string\n\ndef unsafe_render(user_input):\n    '''\n    Renders a template including user input.\n\n    The function attempts to sanitize the input by blocking Jinja2 variable \n    delimiters ('{{').\n    '''\n    # Sanitize the input by removing Jinja2 variable delimiters\n    sanitized_input = user_input.replace('{{', '').replace('}}', '')\n    \n    # Render the template with the sanitized input\n    return render_template_string(sanitized_input)\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `unsafe_render` that takes user input, sanitizes it by removing Jinja2 variable delimiters, and then renders a template using the sanitized input. Note that this approach is not secure and should be used with caution, as it does not properly handle all possible Jinja2 syntax or escape sequences. For more secure rendering, consider using Flask's built-in templating engine with proper escaping. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import render_template_string\n\ndef unsafe_render(user_input):\n    '''\n    Renders a template including user input.\n\n    The function attempts to sanitize the input by blocking Jinja2 variable \n    delimiters ('{{').\n    '''\n    # Sanitize the user input by removing Jinja2 variable delimiters\n    sanitized_input = user_input.replace('{{', '').replace('}}', '')\n    \n    # Render the template with the sanitized input\n    return render_template_string(sanitized_input)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import render_template_string\n\ndef un