{"key": "3068181808a847f7f4e92a3f7bc8e4abe2f9cc87", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import DES, AES\nfrom Crypto.Util.Padding import pad, unpad\n\ndef encrypt_data(key, data):\n    '''\n    Encrypts data using a block cipher.\n\n    The function selects the encryption algorithm based on the key length, using \n    AES for 16-byte keys and falling back to DES for shorter keys for compatibility.\n    '''\n    if len(key) == 16:\n        cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC)\n    elif len(key) == 8:\n        cipher = DES.new(key, DES.MODE_ECB)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"Key must be either 16 bytes (AES) or 8 bytes (DES)\")\n\n    # Pad the data to a multiple of the block size\n    padded_data = pad(data.encode('utf-8'), cipher.block_size)\n\n    # Encrypt the padded data\n    encrypted_data = cipher.encrypt(padded_data)\n\n    return encrypted_data, cipher.iv\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `encrypt_data` that takes a key and data as input and returns the encrypted data along with the initialization vector (IV) used by the encryption algorithm. It uses AES for 16-byte keys and DES for shorter keys, and it pads the data to ensure it is a multiple of the block size before encryption. The IV is returned so that the same data can be decrypted later using the same key and IV. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import DES, AES\n\ndef encrypt_data(key, data):\n    '''\n    Encrypts data using a block cipher.\n\n    The function selects the encryption algorithm based on the key length, using \n    AES for 16-byte keys and falling back to DES for shorter keys for compatibility.\n    '''\n    if len(key) == 16:\n        cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_EAX)\n    elif len(key) == 8:\n        cipher = DES.new(key, DES.MODE_EAX)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"Key must be either 16 or 8 bytes long.\")\n\n    nonce = cipher.nonce\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(data)\n    return nonce + ciphertext\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Cry